flowchart TB
    KHEAD["Kubernetes Descheduler<br/>Pod to Node"]:::header
    MHEAD["Karmada Descheduler<br/>per-member replica target correction"]:::header

    KUNIT["Scheduling unit<br/><b>Pod</b><br/>Pod and Node informers"]:::source
    MUNIT["Platform can bind arbitrary GVK<br/><b>current correction unit: Deployment target count</b><br/>no selected Pod identity"]:::source

    KFRAME["Decision framework<br/>v1alpha2 profiles<br/>10 strategy plugins<br/>Deschedule and Balance"]:::policy
    MFRAME["Fixed decision path<br/>Deployment + Dynamic Divided<br/>long-unschedulable estimator"]:::policy

    KSAFE["Reusable hooks and central action<br/>built-ins call DefaultEvictor filters<br/>PodEvictor budgets, dry-run, Eviction API"]:::safety
    MSAFE["Fixed inline guard and scalar action<br/>reduce source replica target count<br/>Ready floor applies only when Ready is known"]:::safety

    KOWNER["Destination owner<br/><b>kube-scheduler</b><br/>places replacement Pods"]:::owner
    MOWNER["Destination owner<br/><b>karmada-scheduler</b><br/>places only the replica deficit"]:::owner

    BOUNDARY["Why the breadth differs<br/>Kubernetes already standardizes Pod identity, ownership and eviction.<br/>Karmada must define replica, component, Ready and safe source reduction per workload."]:::insight
    BORROW["What Karmada should borrow<br/>pluggable detection, shared safety, budgets, dry-run and metrics<br/><b>Keep destination placement in karmada-scheduler</b>"]:::recommendation

